<%# A list row's picture: a wide image (16:9), whole and never cropped, in a
    fixed 16:9 box so rows line up. With no wide image the same box carries
    the name's two letters on pink, the way a production without a poster is
    drawn on the Productions list (Tim, 2026-11-08: a blank space there "is
    just garbage"). Wide ones only, never the poster.
    Locals: image (a variant, or nil), name (alt, and the letters), width
    (Tailwind width classes, default "w-20"). %>
<%
  width = local_assigns.fetch(:width, "w-20")
  image = local_assigns[:image]
  name = local_assigns[:name].to_s
%>
<% if image %>
  <div class="<%= width %> flex-shrink-0 aspect-video rounded overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 bg-white">
    <%= image_tag image, alt: name, class: "w-full h-full object-contain" %>
  </div>
<% else %>
  <div class="<%= width %> flex-shrink-0 aspect-video rounded bg-pink-100 flex items-center justify-center" aria-hidden="true" data-wide-thumb-letters>
    <span class="text-sm font-bold text-pink-600"><%= Monogram.letters(name) %></span>
  </div>
<% end %>
